      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T15:19:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I can\u0027t really claim to understand all this myself, but apparently \"it\u0027s both\":\n\nIt\u0027s both, and they coincide. Merge keys come from the YAML 1.1 merge type working draft (https://yaml.org/type/merge.html), where merge behaviour attaches to the tag tag:yaml.org,2002:merge; a plain \u003c\u003c acquires that tag by implicit resolution, and !!merge/!\u003ctag:yaml.org,2002:merge\u003e denote it explicitly via core tag syntax. So the tagged forms follow from the type definition rather than being a yaml.v3 quirk — yaml.v3 supports them, and our merge.test golden data has pinned them since 2018 (it originally came from go-yaml\u0027s own test suite), so dropping them would be a permanent regression once the old decoder is removed, not something the experiment transition smooths over. Concretely, goccy v1.19.2 rejects !!merge \"\u003c\u003c\" with a parse error and parses the other tagged forms as a plain tag node, losing the merge semantics.\n\nI shall file a bug upstream.",
      "parentUuid": "bda2196f_4d96558e",
      "revId": "eb382f79f17b74cb8b8dceef7d9e5e611d25ad18",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
