      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T15:19:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Erm, see your commit 4fe848db9 ;)\n\nFor a scalar like 0778, YAML 1.1 resolution fails as int (bad octal digits) and fails as 1.1 float (which requires a dot), so most 1.1 decoders resolve it as a string. yaml.v3 is the odd one out: its resolver falls through int and then matches its own float regexp (plain digits qualify), so it resolves 0778 as float 778.\n\n\u003e Before Daniel\u0027s 2024 commit 4fe848db9, the old CUE decoder took yaml.v3\u0027s float tag at face value and then choked building a CUE literal from the original text, because CUE decimals can\u0027t start with 0\n\nExactly this code exists at yaml/decode.go:785",
      "parentUuid": "63d92879_3c6423d0",
      "revId": "eb382f79f17b74cb8b8dceef7d9e5e611d25ad18",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89114165_801cc998",
        "filename": "internal/encoding/yaml/goccy/decode.go",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 1529,
      "author": {
        "id": 1017720
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T07:58:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m a little nervous about this. We want the new decoder to have nice semantics when decoding spec-compliant YAML into CUE; matching the behavior of the old decoder is not the desired outcome here, given that the old decoder had bugs, and that we\u0027re providing a CUE_EXPERIMENT transition anyway.\n\nIn other words, having wonky go-yaml/yaml semantics in the new decoder would mean we\u0027d need another CUE_EXPERIMENT in the future to clean this up; I\u0027d rather bite the bullet now.",
      "revId": "eb382f79f17b74cb8b8dceef7d9e5e611d25ad18",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
